{"html":"<p>You wrote two functions that do the same job. Both pass the tests. Which one is better?</p>\n<p>On ten items, you can&#39;t tell. On ten million, one finishes in a blink and the other never seems to end. <strong>Big O notation</strong> is how developers talk about that difference, before it hurts in production or in an interview.</p>\n<p>This guide explains it with plain words, short JavaScript examples, and visualizers you can watch step by step.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-big-o-measures\">What Big O Measures</h2>\n<p>Big O describes <strong>how the work grows when the input grows</strong>. It does not tell you how many milliseconds a function takes: that depends on the machine, the language and the data. It tells you the <em>shape</em> of the growth.</p>\n<p>Say <code>n</code> is the size of the input, like the length of an array.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>If the work stays the same when <code>n</code> doubles, the function is <strong>O(1)</strong>.</li>\n<li>If the work doubles when <code>n</code> doubles, it is <strong>O(n)</strong>.</li>\n<li>If the work is multiplied by four when <code>n</code> doubles, it is <strong>O(n²)</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Two rules make this simple:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Drop the constants.</strong> A loop that runs <code>2n + 10</code> times is O(n). When <code>n</code> is a million, the <code>+ 10</code> and the <code>2</code> don&#39;t change the story.</li>\n<li><strong>Keep the biggest term.</strong> <code>n² + n</code> is O(n²). When <code>n</code> is large, <code>n²</code> is so much bigger that <code>n</code> doesn&#39;t matter.</li>\n</ol>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Big O usually describes the <strong>worst case</strong>: the slowest an algorithm can be for an input of size <code>n</code>. That is the promise you can rely on.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h2 id=\"o-1-constant-time\">O(1): Constant Time</h2>\n<p>The work doesn&#39;t depend on the size of the input. Reading an array item by its index, or a value in a <code>Map</code> by its key, takes the same time with 10 items or 10 million.</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">function</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> first</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">items</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  return</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> items[</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">0</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">];</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">const</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> ages</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> new</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> Map</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">([</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">  [</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"ada\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, </span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">36</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">],</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">  [</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"alan\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, </span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">41</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">],</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">]);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">ages.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">get</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0A3069;--shiki-dark:#A5D6FF\">\"alan\"</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">); </span><span style=\"color:#6E7781;--shiki-dark:#8B949E\">// O(1) on average</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>Pushing to and popping from a <a href=\"/visualizers/stack/\">stack</a> is O(1) too: you only touch the top.</p>\n<h2 id=\"o-log-n-logarithmic-time\">O(log n): Logarithmic Time</h2>\n<p>The work grows by one step each time the input <strong>doubles</strong>. This happens when each step throws away half of what is left.</p>\n<p>The classic example is <a href=\"/visualizers/binary-search/\">binary search</a> in a sorted array: look at the middle, then keep only the half that can hold the value.</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">function</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> binarySearch</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">sorted</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, </span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">target</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  let</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> low </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 0</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  let</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> high </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> sorted.</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">length</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> -</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 1</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  while</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (low </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">&#x3C;=</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> high) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">    const</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> middle</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> Math.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">floor</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">((low </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">+</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> high) </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">/</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 2</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">    if</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (sorted[middle] </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">===</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> target) </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">return</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> middle;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">    if</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (sorted[middle] </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">&#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> target) low </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> middle </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">+</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 1</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">    else</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> high </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> middle </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">-</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 1</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">  }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  return</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> -</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">1</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>On a million items, that is at most about <strong>20 steps</strong>. On a billion, about 30. That is why O(log n) feels almost as fast as O(1).</p>\n<h2 id=\"o-n-linear-time\">O(n): Linear Time</h2>\n<p>The work grows at the same pace as the input. You look at each item once, or a fixed number of times.</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">function</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> sum</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">numbers</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  let</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> total </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 0</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  for</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">const</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> number</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> of</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> numbers) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    total </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">+=</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> number;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">  }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  return</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> total;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>Finding the largest value, counting words, or searching an <strong>unsorted</strong> array are all O(n): in the worst case, the item you want is the last one.</p>\n<h2 id=\"o-n-log-n-linearithmic-time\">O(n log n): Linearithmic Time</h2>\n<p>This is the cost of the fast, general sorting algorithms. <a href=\"/visualizers/merge-sort/\">Merge sort</a> splits the array in half again and again (that is the <code>log n</code> part), then merges every level back together (that is the <code>n</code> part).</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">function</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> mergeSort</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">items</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  if</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (items.</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">length</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> &#x3C;=</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 1</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">return</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> items;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  const</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> middle</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> Math.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">floor</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(items.</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">length</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> /</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 2</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  const</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> left</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> mergeSort</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(items.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">slice</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">0</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, middle));</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  const</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> right</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> mergeSort</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(items.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">slice</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(middle));</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  const</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> merged</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> [];</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  let</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> i </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 0</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  let</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> j </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 0</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  while</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (i </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">&#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> left.</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">length</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> &#x26;&#x26;</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> j </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">&#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> right.</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">length</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    merged.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">push</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(left[i] </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">&#x3C;=</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> right[j] </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">?</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> left[i</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">++</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">] </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">:</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> right[j</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">++</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">]);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">  }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  return</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> [</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">...</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">merged, </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">...</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">left.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">slice</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(i), </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">...</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">right.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">slice</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(j)];</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p><code>Array.prototype.sort</code> in modern JavaScript engines is O(n log n) as well. As a rule of thumb, <strong>you can&#39;t sort faster than O(n log n)</strong> by comparing items.</p>\n<h2 id=\"o-n-quadratic-time\">O(n²): Quadratic Time</h2>\n<p>The work grows with the square of the input. It usually comes from a <strong>loop inside a loop</strong> over the same data.</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">function</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> hasDuplicate</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">items</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  for</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">let</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> i </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 0</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">; i </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">&#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> items.</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">length</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">; i</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">++</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">    for</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">let</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> j </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">=</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> i </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">+</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 1</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">; j </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">&#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> items.</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\">length</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">; j</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">++</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">      if</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (items[i] </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">===</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> items[j]) </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">return</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> true</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">  }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  return</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> false</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>With 1,000 items, that is about half a million comparisons. With 100,000 items, about <strong>5 billion</strong>. Simple sorts like <a href=\"/visualizers/bubble-sort/\">bubble sort</a>, <a href=\"/visualizers/selection-sort/\">selection sort</a> and <a href=\"/visualizers/insertion-sort/\">insertion sort</a> are O(n²): watch how many swaps they need compared with merge sort.</p>\n<p>The good news: a <code>Set</code> turns this example into O(n), because checking a <code>Set</code> is O(1) on average.</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">function</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> hasDuplicate</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">items</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  const</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> seen</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> new</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> Set</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">();</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  for</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">const</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> item</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> of</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> items) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">    if</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (seen.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">has</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(item)) </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">return</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> true</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">    seen.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">add</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(item);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">  }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  return</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> false</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p>This trade, <strong>a little more memory for a lot less time</strong>, is one of the most common answers in coding interviews.</p>\n<h2 id=\"o-2-exponential-time\">O(2ⁿ): Exponential Time</h2>\n<p>The work <strong>doubles</strong> each time the input grows by one. It shows up when a function calls itself twice for each step, without remembering results.</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">function</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> fibonacci</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">n</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  if</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (n </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">&#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 2</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">return</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> n;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  return</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> fibonacci</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(n </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">-</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 1</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">+</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> fibonacci</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(n </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">-</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 2</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><p><code>fibonacci(30)</code> makes more than a million calls. <code>fibonacci(50)</code> would make billions of billions. Remembering the results you already computed, called <strong>memoization</strong>, brings it down to O(n):</p>\n<div data-code-panel><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light-default github-dark-default code-block\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">function</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> fibonacci</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(</span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">n</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, </span><span style=\"color:#953800;--shiki-dark:#FFA657\">memo</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> new</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> Map</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">()) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  if</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (n </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">&#x3C;</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 2</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">) </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">return</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> n;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  if</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> (memo.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">has</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(n)) </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">return</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> memo.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">get</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(n);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  const</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> value</span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> fibonacci</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(n </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">-</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 1</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, memo) </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">+</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\"> fibonacci</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(n </span><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">-</span><span style=\"color:#0550AE;--shiki-dark:#79C0FF\"> 2</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">, memo);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">  memo.</span><span style=\"color:#8250DF;--shiki-dark:#D2A8FF\">set</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">(n, value);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#CF222E;--shiki-dark:#FF7B72\">  return</span><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\"> value;</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#1F2328;--shiki-dark:#E6EDF3\">}</span></span></code></pre><button type=\"button\" data-copy-code>Copy</button></div><h2 id=\"how-they-compare\">How They Compare</h2>\n<p>How many steps each class needs, roughly, as <code>n</code> grows:</p>\n<div data-table-scroll><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>n</th>\n<th>O(1)</th>\n<th>O(log n)</th>\n<th>O(n)</th>\n<th>O(n log n)</th>\n<th>O(n²)</th>\n<th>O(2ⁿ)</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>10</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>10</td>\n<td>33</td>\n<td>100</td>\n<td>1,024</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>100</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>7</td>\n<td>100</td>\n<td>664</td>\n<td>10,000</td>\n<td>31 digits</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>1,000</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>10</td>\n<td>1,000</td>\n<td>9,966</td>\n<td>1,000,000</td>\n<td>302 digits</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>1,000,000</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>20</td>\n<td>1,000,000</td>\n<td>19,931,569</td>\n<td>10¹²</td>\n<td>way too many</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p>If a computer does about a billion simple steps per second, O(n²) on a million items takes <strong>about 17 minutes</strong>. O(n log n) takes <strong>0.02 seconds</strong>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"space-complexity\">Space Complexity</h2>\n<p>Big O works for memory too. <strong>Space complexity</strong> counts the extra memory a function needs as the input grows, not counting the input itself.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>sum</code> above keeps one number: <strong>O(1)</strong> space.</li>\n<li>The <code>Set</code> version of <code>hasDuplicate</code> may store every item: <strong>O(n)</strong> space.</li>\n<li>Merge sort builds new arrays while it merges: <strong>O(n)</strong> space.</li>\n<li>A recursive function also uses memory for each call that is still waiting: recursion <code>n</code> levels deep is O(n) space.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"cheat-sheet-for-common-operations\">Cheat Sheet for Common Operations</h2>\n<div data-table-scroll><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Operation</th>\n<th>Time</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>Read <code>array[i]</code></td>\n<td>O(1)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>push</code> and <code>pop</code> at the end of an array</td>\n<td>O(1)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>shift</code> and <code>unshift</code> at the start</td>\n<td>O(n)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>includes</code>, <code>indexOf</code>, <code>find</code> on an array</td>\n<td>O(n)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>get</code>, <code>set</code>, <code>has</code> on a <code>Map</code> or <code>Set</code></td>\n<td>O(1)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sort an array</td>\n<td>O(n log n)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Binary search in a sorted array</td>\n<td>O(log n)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Insert into a <a href=\"/visualizers/binary-heap/\">binary heap</a></td>\n<td>O(log n)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"/visualizers/breadth-first-search/\">Breadth-first search</a> on a graph</td>\n<td>O(V + E)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p><code>V</code> and <code>E</code> are the number of vertices and edges: graph algorithms often have more than one input size.</p>\n<h2 id=\"how-to-find-the-big-o-of-your-code\">How to Find the Big O of Your Code</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Find the input</strong> and call its size <code>n</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Count the loops.</strong> One loop over the input is O(n). A loop inside a loop is O(n²). A loop that halves what is left is O(log n).</li>\n<li><strong>Look inside each line.</strong> <code>items.includes(x)</code> inside a loop is a hidden second loop: the whole thing is O(n²).</li>\n<li><strong>Add steps in a row, multiply steps inside each other.</strong> A loop followed by another loop is O(n + n), so O(n). A loop inside a loop is O(n × n).</li>\n<li><strong>Drop the constants and keep the biggest term.</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"common-mistakes\">Common Mistakes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Thinking O(1) means fast.</strong> It means the time doesn&#39;t grow. A constant step that takes a second is still O(1).</li>\n<li><strong>Forgetting built-in methods.</strong> <code>slice</code>, <code>includes</code>, <code>indexOf</code> and the spread operator all go through the array.</li>\n<li><strong>Optimizing too early.</strong> For 50 items, O(n²) is fine. Pick clear code first, and reach for a better complexity when <code>n</code> can get large.</li>\n<li><strong>Ignoring the average case.</strong> <a href=\"/visualizers/quick-sort/\">Quick sort</a> is O(n²) in the worst case, but O(n log n) on average, and often the fastest in practice.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"practice\">Practice</h2>\n<p>The best way to make Big O stick is to watch it happen:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Open the <a href=\"/visualizers/\">visualizers</a> and run bubble sort and merge sort on the same values. Count the steps.</li>\n<li>Try the <a href=\"/interview/algorithms/\">data structures and algorithms interview questions</a> to test yourself, from junior to senior.</li>\n<li>Take a <a href=\"/quiz/\">quiz</a> to check what you know.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Once you start asking <em>&quot;what happens when this list gets 1,000 times bigger?&quot;</em>, you are thinking in Big O.</p>\n"}